Use if, elif, and else to choose which code runs. A for loop repeats over a sequence.

Example:
score = 76
if score >= 70:
    print("You passed")
else:
    print("Keep practicing")

for number in range(3):
    print(number)

A class describes a kind of object. Each instance stores its own data, and methods describe behavior.

Example:
class Book:
    def __init__(self, title):
        self.title = title
        self.checked_out = False

    def check_out(self):
        self.checked_out = True
